1. Development and testing. You may copy, modify and run the Enterprise
   Software, and builds that include it, to develop, test and evaluate
   them. This needs no subscription.

2. Community use. You may copy and run unmodified official FleetOps
   builds that include the Enterprise Software for any purpose, including
   production, without a subscription, as long as no license key is
   installed and the Enterprise features stay off (the Community plan).

3. Enterprise use. Using the Enterprise features for any purpose not
   allowed in section 1, including any production use, needs a valid
   FleetOps Enterprise subscription covering the number of nodes, and the
   license key issued for it. You may not remove, disable or work around
   the license key check or the limits it enforces, or turn on the
   Enterprise features in any other way.

4. Modifications. You may modify the Enterprise Software for the uses
   allowed in sections 1 and 3; section 2 covers unmodified official
   builds only. Contributions you send to the FleetOps project for ee/
   are licensed to the project under these same terms, with the added
   right for the project to relicense them.

5. Distribution. You may not distribute, sublicense, sell, or offer as a
   hosted service the Enterprise Software or modified versions of it.
   Unmodified official FleetOps builds may be copied for your own use
   under section 2 or 3.

6. No warranty. THE ENTERPRISE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT
   WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS
   OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
